  "equipment_type": "Power and energy meter",
  "applies_to": "Schneider Electric PowerLogic PM200-series power meters on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the PowerLogic PM200: 58 objects (39 AI, 12 AO, 7 BI), all polled. Inputs give real, apparent and reactive energy and power, PF, frequency, present and max demand, phase currents and voltages, scale factors, range flags and firmware; outputs hold the demand intervals, CT/PT ratios, system type, units and reset.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Scheider_Power_Meter_PM200_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the maker's Modbus register document (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Schneider%20Electric%20PM200.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "All 58 rows are flagged for polling in the profile, so every object is served to BACnet once the profile is loaded.",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
    "Values are integers scaled by the scale-factor objects AI 30-33 (current, voltage, power, energy)."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Scheider_Power_Meter_PM200_a",
    "doc_number": "Scheider_Power_Meter_PM200_a_LX.csv",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Schneider%20Electric%20PM200.zip"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Map total real power, real energy consumption and voltage A-B first. The listed objects are read-only.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AI 4",
        "name": "Total Real Power",
        "why": "Total real power"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "Real Energy Consumption",
        "why": "Real energy consumption"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 24",
        "name": "Voltage Phase A-B",
        "why": "Voltage A-B"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 15",
        "name": "Current Instantaneous Phase A",
        "why": "Current A"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 7",
        "name": "Total Power Factor",
        "why": "Total power factor"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 8",
        "name": "Frequency (derived from Phase A)",
        "why": "Frequency"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 9",
        "name": "Total Real Power Present Demand",
        "why": "Real power present demand"
      }
    ],
    "enable": null,
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "The BASgatewayLX presents each Modbus device as its own virtual BACnet device on BACnet IP; give it a unique device instance and Modbus address (serial) or IP address (Modbus TCP) when you add it with this profile.",
      "One BASgatewayLX handles up to 100 Modbus devices and 1000 polled points in total, so leave unneeded rows unpolled."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "CT/PT ratio and system type outputs are meter setup; writing them changes every reading."
    ]
  },
